<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Realm of Jovan Nenad</h1><p class="st-meta">1526 CE – 1527 CE · capital Subotica</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Brief Serbian realm in the southern Hungarian plain, created by the self-proclaimed tsar Jovan Nenad in the chaos after the battle of Mohács.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Ottoman victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs">Mohács</a> in 1526, a Serbian adventurer known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jovan-nenad">Jovan Nenad</a>, the Black Man, gathered an army of Serbian refugees and peasants in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/backa">Bačka</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> that may have numbered 15,000. He drove off Ottoman raiders, took control of the region and proclaimed himself tsar, setting up his court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subotica">Subotica</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>His realm was a military regime resting on his army, which lived from the land and from requisitions on Hungarian nobles. In the contest for the Hungarian throne <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jovan-nenad">Jovan Nenad</a> first backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a>, then switched to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand of Habsburg</a>. His claim to a Serbian imperial title and his origins remain obscure, and contemporary accounts are partisan.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">Zápolya</a>'s forces defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jovan-nenad">Jovan Nenad</a> in the summer of 1527, and he was killed soon afterwards near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szeged">Szeged</a>. His army dispersed and the region fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> within a few years. Serbian tradition remembers him as a forerunner of later Serbian autonomy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vojvodina">Vojvodina</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1526 CE – 1527 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.07%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1526 CE – 1527 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Subotica</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jovan Nenad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Serbian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Empire of Jovan Nenad, Tsardom of Jovan Nenad</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1526&amp;focus=realm-of-jovan-nenad" aria-label="Realm of Jovan Nenad on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5144 555 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Realm of Jovan Nenad lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5464 811L5446 783M5464 811L5445 769"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5446 783h0M5445 769h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5464 811h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5464 811h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Subotica. <a href="/atlas?year=1526&amp;focus=realm-of-jovan-nenad">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
